            <ArticleTitle>[A rare cause of talalgia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>168</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11604/pamj.2017.26.168.11553</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Talalgie is one of the most common symptoms involving the foot. Intra-bone lipoma is one of the most rare bone tumors of the calcaneus. We report the case of a patient presenting with intermittent and spontaneous chronic heel pain. Clinical and radiological examinations confirmed the diagnosis of lipoma of the calcaneus. This study aimed to educate clinicians about the existence of this rare lesion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
